PARITY (web GotoIndicator.tsx → native)
  Web source is a passive controlled indicator:
      function GotoIndicator({ visible }) {
        const { t } = useTranslation();
        if (!visible) return null;
        return <div …fixed bottom-20 …bg(surface-overlay) backdrop-blur-xl border …>
          <span>{t('shortcuts.goto','Go to...')}</span><kbd>g</kbd><span>+</span><kbd>?</kbd>
        </div>;
      }
  Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seam, no HTTP in the view):
    visible (prop)         → GotoIndicatorSource emits GotoIndicatorInput (the controlled visibility —
                             Bool?, nil = not yet resolved — plus the controller's load / connectivity
                             state); the view never reads the controller directly.
    useTranslation         → GotoStrings P1/S10 facade (every literal keyed, incl. the key-cap glyphs and
                             the "+" separator the web hardcodes in JSX).
    useMotionPreference     → @Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion): the pill's slide-in/fade-in
                             entrance (web `slide-in-from-bottom + fade-in`) collapses to opacity/instant,
                             and the shared TSSkeleton shimmer (loading) is already RM-gated.
  Composition: a frosted bottom-anchored pill — web `bg(surface-overlay) backdrop-blur-xl` → TSMaterial.overlay
               (.thinMaterial) in a Capsule with the token border + a soft shadow; the muted prompt
               ("Go to…") followed by the `g` / `?` key caps (web `<kbd>`: GotoKeyCap, monospaced, on the
               elevated surface tone) separated by a muted `+`. The pill is one VoiceOver element: label =
               the prompt, hint = "Press g then ? to jump to a section." (the `{{keys}}` template filled
               with the spoken chord). The cap glyphs are accessibilityHidden so VO never spells them out.
  i18n keys (web → catalog): shortcuts.goto — present; + the key-cap / separator / conjunction / a11y-hint
               keys, the P4 leaf chrome (loading / empty / error / retry), and the freshness keys.
  States rendered (every one, no hidden surface): loading, empty (web `return null` → friendly card, the
               native improvement, never a blank box), error (web QueryError peer + retry), data (the hint),
               stale, offline (freshness chip + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).

  Native leaf-contract choices (disclosed, consistent with the sibling surfaces 0111/0113/0116):
    • visibility is modelled Bool? so the initial unresolved window is `loading` and a known visibility
      SURVIVES a transient loading/error (the P4 "cached survives" leaf); web has only true/null.
    • the `connection` axis (controller snapshot freshness) is the orthogonal stale/offline chip.

